                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a62ee809-59ad-3d0d-b739-826f24753e29",
                        "entry_id": "e3cc25df-92e9-3279-b327-9d79dd1be622",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A peristyle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "in ancient Roman contexts"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e053193d-2f56-4b97-8d14-7adeee3d417c",
                                "sense_id": "a62ee809-59ad-3d0d-b739-826f24753e29",
                                "text": "A similar design we find in the peristylium of the Casa della Caccia, or di Dedalo e Pasifae, but for its being still more irregular, owing to the want of a rectangular termination; the atrium of this house also is spacious, and perfectly regular."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "51cd6ee3-6ae0-4353-86eb-547dbe34c09c",
                                "sense_id": "a62ee809-59ad-3d0d-b739-826f24753e29",
                                "text": "This house, like many others at the time of the destruction of the city, was undergoing repairs—one of the sides of the peristylium being left unfrescoed, the other being finished."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f97740e1-d83d-41da-97ea-7c00322e9ca7",
                                "sense_id": "a62ee809-59ad-3d0d-b739-826f24753e29",
                                "text": "Yet still the peristylia of lordly mansions were decked with flowers and wreathed with ivy, for it was forbidden to manifest any signs of grief."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4f451ab3-a0f7-4f33-95a0-2f4478653312",
                                "sense_id": "a62ee809-59ad-3d0d-b739-826f24753e29",
                                "text": "\"If she should discover that I had enlisted with slaves and shopkeepers in the Galilean's fellowship\"—Claudia shrugged, left unfinished her observation. She crossed the mosaic of the terrace's paving and entered the peristylium."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1cb80ae2-8d5c-4603-bb0d-bb87c09867ad",
                                "sense_id": "a62ee809-59ad-3d0d-b739-826f24753e29",
                                "text": "Escorted back to the Praetorium building two hours later wearing a simple Roman tunic, Marcellinus was ushered into a peristylium area, a small courtyard open to the sky surrounded by a portico of rough wooden columns."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
